 YUME tunnels application streams through an authenticated TLS 1.3 carrier
 that can use an HTTP/2 camouflage preface.
 .
 This package contains the public C header, pkg-config file, and CMake
 package config for building software against libyume.

Package: yume
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libssl3t64 (>= 3.5.0),
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
 yume-daemon (= ${binary:Version})
Suggests:
 tor,
 yume-gui
Description: stealth transport command-line client
 YUME tunnels application streams through an authenticated TLS 1.3 carrier
 that can use an HTTP/2 camouflage preface. The command-line client supports
 SOCKS mode, local and reverse forwarding, relay features, and optional
 routing through external anonymity networks such as Tor.
 .
 This Debian build links against the system-installed libbasefwx for the
 cryptographic primitives used by the mandatory ML-KEM-1024 + X25519 + PSK
 establishment and directional AES-256-GCM ratchet.

Package: yume-daemon
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libssl3t64 (>= 3.5.0),
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Suggests:
 ssl-cert
Description: stealth transport server daemon
 YUME tunnels application streams through an authenticated TLS 1.3 carrier
 that can use an HTTP/2 camouflage preface.
 .
 This package contains the yumed server daemon, a disabled-by-default
 systemd service, a locked service user, and the default /etc/yume
 configuration directory. It does not start listening on install; operators
 must provide TLS material, authorized client keys, two protected 32-byte
 secret files, and a healthy loopback HTTP cover backend first.

Package: yume-gui
Architecture: any
Build-Profiles: <!nogui>
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 yume (= ${binary:Version})
Recommends:
 libayatana-appindicator3-1
Description: graphical desktop client for the Yume transport
 yume-gui is an optional Dear ImGui-based desktop application that
 embeds the yume_core library directly. It provides client connection
 management, local server hosting, composite Ed25519 + ML-DSA-87 identity and
 authorization key management, a relay directory and chat, log inspection, and a
 system tray icon with minimise-to-tray behaviour.
 .
 This package is independent of the CLI binaries and can be installed
 alongside them. The CLI continues to be the supported automation
 surface; the GUI is for desktop users.
